        "raw": "Hey guys, brand new to the game.  Played the demo at PAX East, loved it, got the game and the expansion and all the cool promo toys.  So I busted it out for a 4 player game with some friends and we drew Omnitron (Note: Probably not the best guy for the first learning game as he has some crazy mechanics) and I know this sounds like the most basic of questions and I did try to search but I can't figure out the start phase vs \"read the text\" phase.\n\nSo each phase for the villain says \"Start\" follow any instructions on any cards in play\nPlay: reveal the top card of the villain deck and play it following any instructions on the card.  Here is where I know it sounds silly but maybe Omnitron only has a majority of Start: cards but do you pull a card and then play it only if there is text not in the Start side or for this particular phase only you play start phase as well.  We kept flip flopping in how we played it because a card would come out, do nothing, and then the heroes would do whatever was necessary for it to go away that turn, so he never really did anything to us, so we thought maybe for the flip you still do it but it just got wierd ;)\n\nHope that makes sense so to sum up:\n\nDuring the Play phase of the villain and environment turn, do you follow any instructions on the card regardless of what comes before it or if the only text on it is a Start: or End: then the card effectively does nothing during the play phase?\n\nThanks!\n\n-Will",
