        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/58956e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-24T14:30:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;xwillybabyx&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"xwillybabyx\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So for example, we played in Megalopolis.  The card says:</p>\n<p>At the start of the environment turn, this card deals the 2 targets with the highest HP 5 melee damage each.</p>\n<p>So we assumed that mean during the play phase, this card does nothing but goes on the table, but we were easily able to deal with it every time so then we thought, well it does say “Play: reveal the card and follow the text” so then we though maybe that means during the play phase even though it says it to do it again.</p>\n<p>-Will</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The text states that it happens at the start of the Environment turn. It is was just played so it is still the play Environment card part of the Environment turn. It would apply at the next Start of the Environment turn. If the Environment card said that the effect would happen at the End of the Environment turn then it would take effect before you could deal with it.</p>",
